---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Request a Part — The Lost Clip Society">
  <section>
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <div class="eyebrow">Request a part</div>
      <h1>Tell us what your dealer laughed at.</h1>
      <p>
        Give us the car and the part — a part number if you have one, a description and a photo
        if you don’t. We’ll trace its OEM paper trail and add it to the catalog. Then, depending
        on what exists in the world, we’ll tell you exactly what it takes to make yours.
      </p>
      <div class="tiers">
        <div class="tier"><b>You have the old part (even broken)?</b> Best case — we measure it
          and reproduce it. Mail-in or guided self-measurement.</div>
        <div class="tier"><b>Part’s still on the car but stuck there?</b> We’ll guide you through
          in-place photos, a few caliper readings, and — for sockets and holes — a $5 putty
          impression that captures what matters.</div>
        <div class="tier"><b>Part’s gone entirely?</b> The interfaces it clipped into are still
          on your car, and those are what determine fit. Shape comes from records; fit comes
          from your car. We’ll source a donor if one exists.</div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        The request form is coming online with the shop. Until then:
        <a href="mailto:requests@lostclipsociety.com">requests@lostclipsociety.com</a> — include
        year, model, and your best description. Photos welcome. Laughter optional.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 720px; }
  h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin: 8px 0 var(--space-4); }
  p { color: var(--fg-dim); }
  .tiers { display: grid; gap: var(--space-3); margin: var(--space-4) 0; }
  .tier {
    background: var(--bg-2); border: var(--border-hairline) solid var(--edge);
    padding: var(--space-4); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--fg-dim);
  }
  .tier b { color: var(--fg); display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; font-family: var(--font-display); }
  .note a { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
